describe_data: description, inputSchema  +or properties -display units, -bands), +bands, aggregates), -class +class, verified `examples` -"nbm_conus"}. +"<from search_data>"}.  parameters: -Pipeline +A -identifier (e.g. "nbm_conus", "mrms_reflectivity_conus"). Discover valid values with search_data; inspect variables with describe_data. Length: 1-80 characters. +id from search_data or get_data (1-80 characters).
find_places: inputSchema, outputSchema  parameters: +input.include input.include description: boundaries: each row's state, county and zone ids for get_data's area. input.include enum: ["boundaries"] +output.candidates.boundaries output.candidates.boundaries description: With include boundaries: containing-boundary ids per reference layer (state, county, zone, office), each an `area` reference get_data takes as {product, feature_id}.
find_tools: description  -comparisons, forecast totals, +routes, -people at risk;
get_data: description, outputSchema  -Values of +Values, totals, comparisons, people and POI counts from -grid or snapshot -(NBM, HRRR, RRFS, GFS, RTMA, MRMS, air quality, ...) +(models, radar, alerts, outlooks, reference layers) -or reduced -inline area: series, stats per step bucket, +area, -windows where conditions hold. +as items. -tokens from search_data and describe_data; +or `product:property` tokens, a standard name or a concept such as `population`; +(an `area` reference is `{product, feature_id}`) -forecast +`stats` reduces per `step` or over the area; -catalog  parameters: +output.next_cursor description: With one element, or a call that reads only grids and snapshots: resend the same call with this as `cursor`. Otherwise each element carries its own. -place), +place or area), +output.results.area output.results.area description: The area an element answers: a reference ({product, feature_id | filter}) or an inline one. +output.results.entitlement output.results.entitlement description: With entitlement_required: what is withheld and the flag that grants it. output.results.features output.results.features description: features: this page of matching features. ou
get_observed_precipitation: description  -get_period_totals (planning); +get_data (catalog);
search_data: description, inputSchema, outputSchema  -why and +why, -(ready for "now"; `time_start`/`time_end` or `at` for a past time); +and any verified `example`;  parameters: -e.g. "nbm" +describe_data's `family` +output.hits.example output.hits.example description: A verified get_data call on this dataset for a question like this one, verbatim: adapt its place and times. output.hits.example.call output.hits.example.question

create_payment: description  -invoice +lightningInvoice -amount (sats), +amountSats,
get_job_result: description  -segments }; +segments, srt, vtt } (a result too large for one reply comes back without segments, srt and vtt, with resultTruncated, omitted and fullResultUrl: a free link to the whole result);
transcribe_audio: description  -Up +Priced per minute of audio; a 66-minute file works in one call. A result too large for one reply (word timestamps pass it after a few minutes of audio) comes back without segments, srt and vtt, with fullResultUrl: a free link -500 MB / 60 minutes per file. +the whole result.
